// ============================================================================
// MATHEMATICAL BACKGROUND & COORDINATE REPRESENTATION:
//
// 1. Continuous C5 Model vs. Discrete Rational Polyhedron:
//    - The idealized geometric counterexample candidate #229 has continuous
//      5-fold rotational symmetry (C5) about the z-axis generated by rotating
//      4 seed vertices:
//        seed 0 (top cap), seed 1 (upper ring), seed 2 (middle ring), seed 3 (lower ring)
//      by increments of 2*pi/5 (72 degrees).
//    - The rotation matrix R_z(2*pi/5) involves cos(2*pi/5) = (sqrt(5) - 1)/4
//      and sin(2*pi/5) = sqrt((5 + sqrt(5))/8). These trigonometric values are
//      irrational algebraic numbers in Q(sqrt(5), sqrt(10 + 2*sqrt(5))).
//    - Consequently, even if seed vertices 0..3 have exact rational (or algebraic)
//      coordinates, their continuous C5 orbit points for k in {1, 2, 3, 4} are
//      IRRATIONAL in R^3 and cannot be represented exactly in Q^3.
//
// 2. The Frozen Rational Polytope in Lean 4 and C++ Tools:
//    - The Rupert/Nopert property is certified over a SPECIFIC, RIGID rational
//      polyhedron P in Q^3 with exactly 20 vertices.
//    - To avoid algebraic number fields and keep Lean 4 kernel verification
//      fast, decodable, and certified via exact rational Farkas cages, the 20
//      vertices are frozen as fixed rational numbers in Q^3.
//    - Vertices 0..3 are the rational seed points.
//    - Vertices 4..19 are high-precision rational approximations (matching to
//      16 decimal digits, error < 3e-16) to the continuous C5 orbit points.
//    - In Lean (Noperthedron.Nopert229.Vertices), the formalization defines both:
//        a) `exactVertex` in R^3: continuous C5 rotation of the 4 seed vertices.
//        b) `rationalVertices` in Q^3: the frozen rational coordinates below.
//      Lean proves bounds between the rational polyhedron and the ideal continuous
//      model, while our identity tube certification operates directly and strictly
//      on the rational polyhedron P.
//
// 3. Double-Precision Floating Point (VERTICES):
//    - The double array `VERTICES` contains IEEE-754 binary64 approximations
//      matching the exact rational fractions `VERTICES_Q` to < 1e-15 precision.
//    - Both double and rational representations exhibit approximate C5 symmetry
// ============================================================================
// NOTE / REGENERATION:
// The canonical 27-facet rational coordinates with power-of-two denominators
// (2^52) and exact quad planarization (defect = 0 in Q^3) are implemented in
// ruperts/codebdd229.cc (GenerateBestPossibleRationalVertices).
// Drop-in replacements are generated at:
//   - C++:  vertices229_exact27.h
//   - Lean: vertices229_exact27.lean
//   - JSON: vertices229_exact27.json
// See noteperts/QUAD_FACES.md for full analysis and derivation.
// ============================================================================

